Insurance Sales. Massachusetts banks may engage in insurance sales activities if the Commissioner has approved a plan of operation for insurance activities and the bank obtains a license from the Massachusetts Division of Insurance. A bank may be licensed directly or indirectly through an affiliate or a subsidiary corporation established for this purpose. The Bank does not currently sell insurance products, and has not sought approval for direct insurance sales activities. The Bank is licensed to solicit and refer potential insurance customers to an unaffiliated, third-party licensed insurance producer.
