Under current Massachusetts law, the Bank can establish a branch in Massachusetts or in any other state. All branch applications require prior approval of the Commissioner and the FDIC. Finally, the Bank may also establish banking offices in other states by merging with banks or by purchasing banking offices of other banks in other states, subject to certain restrictions.
