Acquisitions. Prior approval from the Commissioner and Federal Reserve Board is required in order for the Bank to acquire another bank. Well capitalized and well managed banks may acquire other banks in any state, subject to certain deposit concentration limits and other conditions, pursuant to the Riegle-Neal Interstate Banking and Branching Efficiency Act of 1994, as amended by the Dodd-Frank Act.
